// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
; specs/turbobaby/webapp_bridge.t27 -- the client half of an authenticated call, and the DTO
; mirror that has to stay shape-compatible with the server.
; The boundary is one browser tab. Inward from the host: where the proof of identity comes from,
; what it is worth, and what the client does in a tab that has no Telegram host at all. Outward
; to the server: what is attached to a request, what happens when one fails, whether a second
; attempt can become a second order, and how long a call may hang. Inward again from the wire:
; what a DTO does when the server stops sending a field. This file owns the CLIENT side of each
; of those and no server rule: whether a request PROVED who it is belongs to request_identity.t27,
; the read API's wire shape and numerals belong to catalog_api.t27, the idempotency verdict
; belongs to commerce.t27, what a customer is told when a call fails belongs to
; client_errors.t27, and which link lands where belongs to deeplink.t27. Five edges, named by ID
; below, not one of them restated.
; --
; WHY (measured 2026-09-21). This half of the product has no compiler in the host test suite.
; src/lib.rs:17 gates `pub mod ui` on target_arch = "wasm32", so `cargo test` compiles none of it
; -- tests/money_is_never_invented.rs:10-16 says exactly that in its own words, and adds that the
; only other compiler, the wasm clippy gate, "has no opinion about unwrap_or(0.0)". The size of
; the blind spot is countable: src/ui holds FIVE `#[cfg(test)]` modules (src/ui/api/local_client.rs:181,
; src/ui/lang.rs:135, src/ui/screens/bike_detail.rs:599, src/ui/screens/catalog_screen.rs:966,
; src/ui/share.rs:409) containing THIRTY-TWO `#[test]` functions, and not one of the thirty-two is
; ever compiled, let alone run. The instrument that does exist is a text scan for four literal
; spellings of unwrap_or. A contract is the only other instrument available here, which is why the
; numbers below are line citations into src/ and never test names.
; The second number that forced the file: NINE call sites attach the identity header across the
; two transport modules, and SEVEN of the nine attach the label that tells the server which kind
; of client sent it. The two that omit it are named below.
; --
; WHERE THE BRIEF IS REFUTED. Six corrections, each measured 2026-09-21.
;   1. "src/ui/api/http.rs (582 lines - retry and timeout)" -- the file has neither. A
;      case-insensitive grep of src/ui/api/http.rs for retry returns 0 and for timeout returns 0,
;      across all 21 of its public functions. The only AUTOMATIC retry in the client half is
;      submit_order_with_retry at src/ui/screens/checkout_screen.rs:128, it wraps exactly one
;      call, and it lives in a screen rather than in the transport. Three other screens carry a
;      retry BUTTON (src/ui/screens/events_screen.rs:920, src/ui/screens/profile_screen.rs:659,
;      src/ui/screens/success_screen.rs:476); those are a customer tap re-arming a resource, not
;      a re-send the code decides on, and they are counted separately. A request deadline does not
;      exist anywhere: AbortController, AbortSignal and .abort() return 0 occurrences over all of
;      src/ui. The twenty-two TimeoutFuture sites in src/ui are animation and polling delays; the
;      one inside the retry loop (:145) is backoff between attempts, not a bound on any attempt.
;   2. The mirror rule is not at risk, it is already refuted, and the count says by how much. Of
;      172 declared fields in src/ui/api/types.rs, 44 carry `#[serde(default)]` -- a plain
;      `grep -c` answers 45, because the comment at :37 names the attribute without being one, so
;      the count below is of attribute lines and not of matches; 27 of those
;      default an Option, where absence stays absence, and SEVEN default a bare number, where
;      absence becomes a zero the server never sent. Three of the seven are the cart's own money
;      and counts: ServerCartItem.quantity (:421), ServerCartItem.unit_price (:423) and
;      ServerCart.total (:435).
;   3. tests/money_is_never_invented.rs:11 cites the wasm gate as `src/lib.rs:16`. Line 16 is
;      blank; the attribute is at :17 and `pub mod ui;` at :18. The claim is right and the
;      citation is ONE line short of the attribute (two short of the module it gates). Recorded
;      because this file leans on that claim.
;   4. The one place the client branches on a duplicated write -- the 409 arm at
;      src/ui/screens/checkout_screen.rs:162-178, whose own comment at :125 calls 409 "already
;      accepted" -- is written against a status POST /api/orders never returns. The server answers
;      a replay with 200 and a body flag (src/api/orders.rs:1245-1249), refuses a malformed key
;      with 400 (:764), and the only StatusCode::CONFLICT in src/api/orders.rs is :2210 in
;      cancel_order. The branch is unreachable from the endpoint it guards.
;   5. The retry's own doc comment miscounts it. src/ui/screens/checkout_screen.rs:124 says
;      "up to 3 attempts (delays 1s, 2s, 4s)", but :140-141 chains one immediate attempt to the
;      three delays, so the ceiling is four requests and not three. The three delays are right;
;      the attempt count is one short, and a reader sizing the worst case from the comment misses
;      one request in every four a single tap can put on POST /api/orders.
;   6. The retry genuinely cannot duplicate a write, but not for a reason visible in the
;      transport. post_json_authed_idempotent_full (src/ui/api/http.rs:209) attaches whatever key
;      it is handed and mints none; the stability comes from the screen, where
;      `k.get_or_insert_with(|| uuid::Uuid::new_v4()...)` at src/ui/screens/checkout_screen.rs:934
;      is the file's only write to that signal. A reader who audits the transport alone cannot
;      establish the property, and the same single write is why an edited cart re-submitted from a
;      mounted screen reuses the key with a different body.
; --
; WHAT THIS FILE NEVER DOES. It publishes no endpoint table: the route table is counted, not
; transcribed, and the path strings that do appear are the two that carry a measured defect. It
; invents no retry count for a call the code does not retry -- one call retries automatically,
; every other call in the transport makes a single attempt, the three manual retry buttons are
; counted as taps and not as re-sends, and that is stated as one and not as an unwritten
; policy. It declares no timeout, because none is implemented; the refusal is recorded instead of
; a plausible number. It re-declares no constant a sibling already holds: the idempotency header
; literal belongs to turbobaby/loyalty-ledger, the initData byte cap and its admission rule to
; turbobaby/request-identity, and this file names both owners rather than copying either value.
; It quotes no shipped string: the Russian comments in src/ui/api/types.rs:374-378 and
; src/ui/api/client.rs:262-268 are cited by path and line and never reproduced. It carries no
; initData sample, real or synthetic, and no telegram id. Nothing from D14 -- no renter, handle,
; phone, key code, plate, debt, purchase price or personal note -- in a constant, a comment or a
; test.
; phi^2 + 1/phi^2 = 3 | TRINITY

module turbobaby-webapp-bridge;

pub const KIND : str = "client-contract";
pub const ID : str = "turbobaby/webapp-bridge";
pub const NAME : str = "TurboBaby Mini App bridge, transport and DTO mirror";
pub const WORLD : str = "gHashTag/turbobaby-user-bot";
pub const MEASURED_AT : str = "2026-09-21";

; --- Sources --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
pub const BRIDGE_SOURCE : str = "src/ui/telegram.rs";
pub const TRANSPORT_SOURCE : str = "src/ui/api/http.rs";
pub const DTO_SOURCE : str = "src/ui/api/types.rs";
pub const TYPED_CLIENT_SOURCE : str = "src/ui/api/client.rs";
pub const SHIM_SOURCE : str = "src/ui/api/local_client.rs";
pub const ROUTE_SOURCE : str = "src/ui/routes.rs";
pub const RETRY_SOURCE : str = "src/ui/screens/checkout_screen.rs";
pub const MIRROR_CONSUMER : str = "src/ui/state.rs";
pub const INSTRUMENT_WITNESS : str = "tests/money_is_never_invented.rs";
; wc -l over the tracked sources, 2026-09-21, so "the whole file" is a measurement.
pub const BRIDGE_SOURCE_LINES : u16 = 811;
pub const TRANSPORT_SOURCE_LINES : u16 = 582;
pub const DTO_SOURCE_LINES : u16 = 454;
pub const TYPED_CLIENT_SOURCE_LINES : u16 = 305;
pub const SHIM_SOURCE_LINES : u16 = 223;
pub const ROUTE_SOURCE_LINES : u16 = 369;

; --- The instrument, declared before anything it measures ------------------------------------
; A contract whose subject no test compiles has to say so first, or every number below reads as
; if a suite stood behind it. None does.
pub const WASM_GATE_SITE : str = "src/lib.rs:17";
pub const SURVEY_CITED_THE_GATE_AT : str = "src/lib.rs:16";
pub const HOST_SUITE_COMPILES_THIS_HALF : bool = false;
pub const CFG_TEST_MODULES_IN_UI : u8 = 5;
pub const UNIT_TESTS_NEVER_COMPILED : u8 = 32;
pub const SHIPPED_INSTRUMENT_IS_A_TEXT_SCAN : bool = true;
pub const SCAN_NEEDLE_COUNT : u8 = 4;
pub const SCAN_SEES_A_DEFAULTED_ZERO : bool = false;
pub const SCAN_GAP_NOTE : str = "tests/money_is_never_invented.rs:116-119 requires one of four literal spellings of unwrap_or on the line. The mirror's own fabricated zero has none: src/ui/api/types.rs:423 carries a serde attribute and no expression at all, and src/ui/state.rs:50 writes a bare 0.0 on its own line inside an else arm, with no money word beside it. Both sites are inside the scanned corpus and invisible to the scan. Closing this needs an instrument that reads the type, not the text.";

pub fn a_claim_here_rests_on_a_test(host_suite_compiles: bool) bool {
  return host_suite_compiles;
}

; --- Ownership edges --------------------------------------------------------------------------
; The pinned compiler lowers a brace import to an empty UseDecl and the gate rejects it, so a
; cross-contract edge is a string naming the owner's ID plus a test asserting the literal. Each
; edge below is named by the OWNER'S DECLARATION NAME and never by a line in the owner's file.
; request-identity owns who a request is. It holds init_data_size_admits and INIT_DATA_MAX_BYTES,
;   which this file mirrors by naming the owner and not the value; it holds lenient_cohort, whose
;   only input is the label this file decides whether to send; and it holds identity_of_request,
;   which this file consumes as a boolean and never recomputes.
; catalog-api owns the read API's wire shape and its numerals. It holds catalog_api_dto_valid,
;   the server's judgement on a response body. This file declares the CLIENT's reaction to a body
;   that has already left the server, which is a different question and the only half it can see.
; commerce owns the idempotency verdict. It holds commerce_idempotency_decision and the five
;   outcomes that decision names, among them the replay and the conflict. This file restates no
;   arm of it: it declares only whether the client attaches a key and whether that key is stable,
;   and takes the verdict as an abstract boolean.
; client-errors owns what the customer is told. It holds render_kind and checkout_message_source.
;   This file counts response classes for the retry rule and maps none of them to a sentence.
; deeplink owns the link grammar and the entry points. It holds LEGACY_ROUTE_ALIASES and
;   deeplink_landing. This file counts the route table's arms and names none of the aliases.
pub const REUSES_REQUEST_IDENTITY_ID : str = "turbobaby/request-identity";
pub const REUSES_CATALOG_API_ID : str = "turbobaby/catalog-api";
pub const REUSES_COMMERCE_ID : str = "turbobaby/commerce";
pub const REUSES_CLIENT_ERRORS_ID : str = "turbobaby/client-errors";
pub const REUSES_DEEPLINK_ID : str = "turbobaby/deeplink";
pub const REUSE_EDGE_COUNT : u8 = 5;
pub const IDENTITY_VERDICT_INPUT : str = "identity_of_request, supplied by the request-identity contract";
pub const COHORT_INPUT_NAME : str = "lenient_cohort, whose reconstructed_header_set is set by this file";
pub const IDEMPOTENCY_VERDICT_INPUT : str = "commerce_idempotency_decision, supplied by the commerce contract";
pub const SIZE_CAP_IS_OWNED_BY : str = "turbobaby/request-identity";
pub const HEADER_NAME_IS_ALREADY_DECLARED_AT : str = "turbobaby/loyalty-ledger";
; The five counted edges are the owners this file DEFERS A QUESTION to -- a question its own
; subject touches and it refuses to answer. That is the criterion, and it is not "supplies a
; parameter": only request-identity and commerce hand this file an abstract input, while
; catalog-api, client-errors and deeplink are deferred a question and hand back nothing. The two
; declarations above are neither: no question passes to loyalty-ledger, only a literal this file
; declines to copy, and request-identity is counted for its deferred questions and not for the
; cap. So neither line below is a sixth edge, and both are recorded so a later reader does not
; add the copy.
pub const CAP_VALUE_IS_RESTATED_HERE : bool = false;
pub const HEADER_LITERAL_IS_RESTATED_HERE : bool = false;
pub const IDEMPOTENCY_ARMS_ARE_RESTATED_HERE : bool = false;
pub const ROUTE_ALIASES_ARE_RESTATED_HERE : bool = false;

; --- Where initData comes from -----------------------------------------------------------------
; get_init_data (src/ui/telegram.rs:573-620) is a single js_sys::eval with three exits, and they
; are not three degrees of the same thing. :578 returns the signed string Telegram supplied.
; :595-611 rebuilds a payload out of initDataUnsafe when the signed string is missing, sorting
; the keys itself and dropping receiver and chat (:598-601); the comment at :582-588 states, in
; the code's own words, that this "can NEVER pass signature validation" and that JSON.stringify
; "cannot reproduce the exact bytes Telegram signed". :614 returns the empty string, and that is
; the exit taken by a browser tab with no Telegram host, because the whole body sits inside the
; `window.Telegram && window.Telegram.WebApp` test at :575.
pub const ORIGIN_NONE : u8 = 0;
pub const ORIGIN_SIGNED : u8 = 1;
pub const ORIGIN_REBUILT : u8 = 2;
pub const ORIGIN_COUNT : u8 = 3;
pub const REBUILT_PAYLOAD_IS_SENT_ANYWAY : bool = true;
pub const REBUILT_PAYLOAD_CAN_VERIFY : bool = false;
pub const KEYS_DROPPED_FROM_THE_REBUILD : u8 = 2;
pub const ABSENT_HOST_YIELDS_AN_EMPTY_STRING : bool = true;
pub const ABSENT_HOST_YIELDS_AN_ERROR : bool = false;

pub fn init_data_origin(host_present: bool, signed_string_present: bool, unsafe_hash_present: bool) u8 {
  if (!host_present) {
    return ORIGIN_NONE;
  }
  if (signed_string_present) {
    return ORIGIN_SIGNED;
  }
  if (unsafe_hash_present) {
    return ORIGIN_REBUILT;
  }
  return ORIGIN_NONE;
}

pub fn origin_is_known(origin: u8) bool {
  return origin == ORIGIN_NONE or origin == ORIGIN_SIGNED or origin == ORIGIN_REBUILT;
}

pub fn init_data_payload_is_empty(origin: u8) bool {
  return origin == ORIGIN_NONE;
}

; A rebuilt payload is a compatibility artefact, not a proof. Whether a proof that reaches the
; server is ACCEPTED is request-identity's question; this is only what the client is holding.
pub fn init_data_can_prove_identity(origin: u8) bool {
  return origin == ORIGIN_SIGNED;
}

; --- What the client does when the bridge is absent ----------------------------------------------
; Nothing stops the call. The empty string flows to every authed helper, and only two sites in
; the whole client half test it: src/ui/api/client.rs:60 omits the header when it is empty, and
; src/ui/api/http.rs:367 does the same inside AdminAuth. Every one of the seven free functions in
; src/ui/api/http.rs sends the header with an empty value instead. The request is made either
; way and the refusal arrives from the server.
pub const EMPTINESS_TEST_SITES : u8 = 2;
pub const HELPERS_THAT_SEND_AN_EMPTY_HEADER : u8 = 7;
pub const ABSENT_BRIDGE_BLOCKS_THE_CALL : bool = false;
pub const ABSENT_BRIDGE_IS_REPORTED_TO_THE_CUSTOMER_HERE : bool = false;

pub fn call_is_attempted(origin: u8) bool {
  return origin == ORIGIN_NONE or origin == ORIGIN_SIGNED or origin == ORIGIN_REBUILT;
}

pub fn refusal_comes_from_the_server(origin: u8, call_attempted: bool) bool {
  return call_attempted and !init_data_can_prove_identity(origin);
}

; --- The label, and why the flag alone cannot be read --------------------------------------------
; is_reconstructed_init_data (src/ui/telegram.rs:557-571) is a SECOND eval, run separately from
; the one that produced the payload. It returns false at :562 when a signed string exists and
; false at :565 when there is no host at all, so the flag says "not rebuilt" for both a genuine
; proof and a browser tab with nothing in it. The server reads the header at src/api/auth.rs:577
; and defaults a missing one to false (:581), which it then logs as "signed-but-invalid" (:588)
; -- the cohort it means to eventually refuse -- rather than "reconstructed-initdata" (:586), the
; cohort it means to keep working. Recovering the origin therefore needs BOTH the label and the
; emptiness of the payload; either alone is ambiguous.
pub const LABEL_ALONE_SEPARATES_ABSENCE_FROM_PROOF : bool = false;
pub const LABEL_IS_READ_BY_A_SECOND_EVAL : bool = true;
pub const AUTH_HEADER_SITES : u8 = 9;
pub const SITES_SENDING_THE_LABEL : u8 = 7;
pub const SITES_OMITTING_THE_LABEL : u8 = 2;
pub const UNLABELLED_SITES : [2]str = ["src/ui/api/http.rs:368", "src/ui/api/client.rs:63"];
pub const MISSING_LABEL_DEFAULTS_TO_TAMPERING : bool = true;

pub fn reconstruction_label(origin: u8) bool {
  return origin == ORIGIN_REBUILT;
}

pub fn origin_recovered_by_receiver(label_set: bool, payload_empty: bool) u8 {
  if (payload_empty) {
    return ORIGIN_NONE;
  }
  if (label_set) {
    return ORIGIN_REBUILT;
  }
  return ORIGIN_SIGNED;
}

; True when the boolean this file hands to the owner's lenient_cohort describes the client that
; actually sent the request. A rebuilt payload with no label is the one false case.
pub fn cohort_input_is_faithful(origin: u8, label_sent: bool) bool {
  if (origin == ORIGIN_REBUILT) {
    return label_sent;
  }
  return true;
}

; --- The size cap, mirrored once and not everywhere ----------------------------------------------
; src/ui/api/client.rs:36-40 replaces an oversize payload with the empty string, which
; with_auth (:60) then declines to send, so the request leaves as an anonymous one. It is the only
; cap on the client: the free functions in src/ui/api/http.rs apply none and send the oversize
; string, which the server refuses at src/api/auth.rs:70. Both the byte value and the admission
; rule are request-identity's; neither is copied here.
pub const CLIENT_CAP_SITES : u8 = 1;
pub const CAP_APPLIES_TO_THE_FREE_HELPERS : bool = false;
pub const OVERSIZE_IS_REFUSED_LOUDLY_ON_THE_CLIENT : bool = false;

pub fn oversize_becomes_anonymous(capped_site: bool, size_admits: bool) bool {
  return capped_site and !size_admits;
}

; --- Retry ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
; submit_order_with_retry (src/ui/screens/checkout_screen.rs:128-199). The loop at :140-141 is
; one immediate attempt chained to the three backoff delays at :136, so four attempts is the
; ceiling and the delay at :145 is skipped on the first. Which classes continue is written into
; the arms: the 2xx arm opens at :153 and returns at :156 or :159, the 409 arm opens at :162 and
; returns at :171 or :177, the 5xx arm opens at :180 and continues at :181, any other status
; returns at :184, and a transport error continues at :187. The class is modelled as constant
; across attempts, which is what the loop assumes when it exhausts the delays.
pub const RETRIED_CALL_COUNT : u8 = 1;
pub const RETRY_SITE : str = "src/ui/screens/checkout_screen.rs:128 submit_order_with_retry";
pub const ATTEMPT_MAX : u8 = 4;
pub const BACKOFF_STEP_COUNT : u8 = 3;
pub const BACKOFF_MS : [3]u16 = [1000, 2000, 4000];
pub const FIRST_ATTEMPT_WAITS : bool = false;
pub const RETRY_LIVES_IN_THE_TRANSPORT : bool = false;
; The doc comment at src/ui/screens/checkout_screen.rs:124 says three. The loop makes four.
pub const ATTEMPTS_CLAIMED_BY_THE_DOC_COMMENT : u8 = 3;
pub const DOC_COMMENT_AGREES_WITH_THE_LOOP : bool = false;
; A retry BUTTON is not a retry. Three screens re-arm a failed resource on a customer tap --
; src/ui/screens/events_screen.rs:920, src/ui/screens/profile_screen.rs:659 and
; src/ui/screens/success_screen.rs:476 -- and none of the three re-sends anything by itself.
; They are counted here so "one call retries" is read as one AUTOMATIC re-send and not as the
; claim that the customer has no way to ask again.
pub const MANUAL_RETRY_BUTTON_SCREENS : u8 = 3;
pub const MANUAL_RETRY_IS_AN_AUTOMATIC_RESEND : bool = false;

pub const CLASS_NETWORK : u8 = 0;
pub const CLASS_SUCCESS : u8 = 1;
pub const CLASS_CONFLICT : u8 = 2;
pub const CLASS_OTHER_STATUS : u8 = 3;
pub const CLASS_SERVER : u8 = 4;
pub const RESPONSE_CLASS_COUNT : u8 = 5;

pub fn response_class_is_known(response_class: u8) bool {
  return response_class <= CLASS_SERVER;
}

pub fn attempt_is_retried(response_class: u8) bool {
  return response_class == CLASS_NETWORK or response_class == CLASS_SERVER;
}

pub fn attempts_used(response_class: u8) u8 {
  if (attempt_is_retried(response_class)) {
    return ATTEMPT_MAX;
  }
  return 1;
}

pub fn backoff_before(attempt_index: u8) u16 {
  if (attempt_index == 0) {
    return 0;
  }
  return BACKOFF_MS[attempt_index - 1];
}

; --- Whether a retry can become a second order ------------------------------------------------
; It cannot, and the reason is not in the transport. The key is minted once per mounted screen at
; src/ui/screens/checkout_screen.rs:934 and that line is the file's only write to the signal, so
; every attempt inside the loop and every later tap carry the same key.
; post_json_authed_idempotent_full (declared at src/ui/api/http.rs:209, attaching the key it was
; handed at :226) mints nothing of its own. The
; same single write is why a customer who edits the cart after a failure and taps again sends the
; old key with a new body: that pairing is what commerce_idempotency_decision resolves, and this
; file names the input rather than the arm.
pub const KEY_IS_ATTACHED_ON_THE_RETRIED_CALL : bool = true;
pub const KEY_IS_MINTED_ONCE_PER_MOUNTED_SCREEN : bool = true;
pub const KEY_WRITE_SITES : u8 = 1;
pub const KEY_IS_REMINTED_AFTER_A_FAILURE : bool = false;
pub const KEY_ROTATES_WHEN_THE_PAYLOAD_CHANGES : bool = false;
pub const KEY_IS_MINTED_BY_THE_TRANSPORT : bool = false;

pub fn retry_can_duplicate_a_write(key_attached: bool, key_stable_across_attempts: bool) bool {
  return !(key_attached and key_stable_across_attempts);
}

pub fn resubmission_reuses_a_key_with_a_new_payload(key_stable: bool, payload_changed: bool, screen_still_mounted: bool) bool {
  return key_stable and payload_changed and screen_still_mounted;
}

; The client never learns which arm the server took. It reads order_id out of a 2xx body
; (src/ui/screens/checkout_screen.rs:155-156) and ignores the idempotent_replay flag the server
; sets beside it at src/api/orders.rs:1248, so a replayed order and a newly created one are
; indistinguishable on this side.
pub const SERVER_REPLAY_STATUS : u16 = 200;
pub const SERVER_REPLAY_FLAG_NAME : str = "idempotent_replay";
pub const CLIENT_READS_THE_REPLAY_FLAG : bool = false;

pub fn client_distinguishes_replay_from_create(reads_replay_flag: bool) bool {
  return reads_replay_flag;
}

; --- The conflict arm that cannot fire ------------------------------------------------------------
; :162-178 treats 409 as "already accepted", fetches /api/orders/user/{id} and returns the first
; element of the array as the order the customer just placed. The list is newest-first --
; src/api/orders.rs:2375 orders by created_at descending -- so the pick is at least the newest
; order, but it is chosen by recency and not by the key that was sent, and nothing checks that it
; is the same order. It does not matter yet, because POST /api/orders never answers 409: the
; replay path returns 200 (src/api/orders.rs:1245), an unusable key returns 400 (:764), and the
; only StatusCode::CONFLICT in that file is cancel_order at :2210. The telegram id used to build
; the recovery URL is itself a fabricated zero when identity is absent
; (src/ui/screens/checkout_screen.rs:1000), so the one path this branch could take would query a
; user that does not exist.
pub const ORDER_CREATE_EVER_RETURNS_409 : bool = false;
pub const CONFLICT_RECOVERY_IS_POSITIONAL : bool = true;
pub const CONFLICT_RECOVERY_MATCHES_THE_KEY : bool = false;
pub const RECOVERY_URL_USES_A_FABRICATED_ID_WHEN_IDENTITY_IS_ABSENT : bool = true;

pub fn conflict_branch_can_fire(server_emits_409_on_create: bool) bool {
  return server_emits_409_on_create;
}

pub fn recovered_order_is_provably_ours(matches_the_key: bool) bool {
  return matches_the_key;
}

; --- Timeout: an honest refusal ---------------------------------------------------------------
; There is no request deadline. AbortController, AbortSignal and .abort() return zero occurrences
; over src/ui, and gloo_net::http::Request is used without one in all 19 request-making functions
; of src/ui/api/http.rs. A hung socket is bounded by the browser and by nothing this repository
; wrote. No number is declared here because none is implemented.
pub const REQUEST_DEADLINE_IS_SHIPPED : bool = false;
pub const ABORT_OCCURRENCES_IN_UI : u8 = 0;
pub const DEADLINE_NOTE : str = "A deadline needs an AbortController per request, a decision about whether a timed-out write may be retried under the same key, and a customer-facing outcome that client-errors would have to map. None of the three exists, so the period stays unstated. The backoff delays inside the retry loop are not a deadline: they space attempts and bound no attempt.";

pub fn request_can_hang_until_the_browser_gives_up(deadline_shipped: bool) bool {
  return !deadline_shipped;
}

; --- The DTO mirror ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
; src/ui/api/types.rs declares 24 structs and 3 enums over 172 fields. A field the server stops
; sending breaks deserialization -- ApiClient::run turns that into ApiError::Parse at
; src/ui/api/client.rs:79 -- UNLESS the field carries `#[serde(default)]`, in which case serde
; writes the type's Default and nothing anywhere notices. 44 fields carry it. For the 27 that
; default an Option the value is None, which is still an absence and still renderable as one. For
; the 7 that default a bare number the value is a zero the server never sent.
pub const DTO_STRUCT_COUNT : u8 = 24;
pub const DTO_ENUM_COUNT : u8 = 3;
pub const DTO_FIELD_COUNT : u16 = 172;
pub const DTO_FIELDS_WITH_A_DEFAULT : u8 = 44;
pub const DEFAULTS_ON_AN_OPTION : u8 = 27;
pub const DEFAULTS_ON_A_BARE_NUMBER : u8 = 7;
pub const DEFAULTS_ON_A_BOOL_STRING_OR_VEC : u8 = 10;
pub const FIELDS_THAT_BREAK_LOUDLY : u16 = 128;
pub const MIRROR_RULE_HOLDS_ON_EVERY_FIELD : bool = false;
pub const UNKNOWN_EXTRA_FIELDS_ARE_IGNORED : bool = true;
pub const NUMERIC_DEFAULT_SITES : [7]str = [
  "src/ui/api/types.rs:28",
  "src/ui/api/types.rs:40",
  "src/ui/api/types.rs:311",
  "src/ui/api/types.rs:421",
  "src/ui/api/types.rs:423",
  "src/ui/api/types.rs:435",
  "src/ui/api/types.rs:446"
];

pub fn dropped_field_breaks_the_client(field_has_serde_default: bool) bool {
  return !field_has_serde_default;
}

pub fn dropped_field_renders_an_invented_value(field_has_serde_default: bool, default_is_a_number: bool) bool {
  return field_has_serde_default and default_is_a_number;
}

pub fn mirror_is_faithful(field_has_serde_default: bool, default_is_a_number: bool) bool {
  return !dropped_field_renders_an_invented_value(field_has_serde_default, default_is_a_number);
}

; --- Where a defaulted number reaches money -----------------------------------------------------
; CartItem::from_server (src/ui/state.rs:32-57) is the only reader of the server cart and it does
; drop what it cannot read: an unrecognised kind at :38 and a zero quantity at :41-43. It does not
; drop an unreadable price. :47-51 replaces a non-finite unit_price with 0.0, and a unit_price the
; server omitted is already 0.0 from the default at src/ui/api/types.rs:423, which is finite and
; passes the test untouched. The line then reaches recalculate_total through the filter_map at
; src/ui/api/http.rs:455 as a free item. The two absences that are loud are loud because the LINE
; disappears; the one that is silent is the price.
pub const LINE_DROPPED_ON_UNKNOWN_KIND : bool = true;
pub const LINE_DROPPED_ON_ZERO_QUANTITY : bool = true;
pub const LINE_DROPPED_ON_AN_ABSENT_PRICE : bool = false;
pub const ABSENT_PRICE_SURVIVES_AS_A_FREE_LINE : bool = true;
pub const NON_FINITE_PRICE_SURVIVES_AS_A_FREE_LINE : bool = true;

pub fn cart_line_survives(kind_known: bool, quantity_positive: bool) bool {
  return kind_known and quantity_positive;
}

pub fn price_absence_is_visible(line_survives: bool, price_field_has_a_default: bool) bool {
  if (!line_survives) {
    return true;
  }
  return !price_field_has_a_default;
}

; --- The route table ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
; src/ui/routes.rs:26-86 declares 26 route arms: 25 named paths and the catch-all `/:..route` at
; :84-85. The catch-all is why an unknown path lands on a screen rather than failing to resolve.
; Which aliases exist and which surface each one lands on is deeplink's, declared there as
; LEGACY_ROUTE_ALIASES; this file counts arms and names none of them.
pub const ROUTE_ARM_COUNT : u8 = 26;
pub const NAMED_ROUTE_COUNT : u8 = 25;
pub const CATCHALL_ROUTE_COUNT : u8 = 1;
pub const ROUTE_TABLE_CAN_FAIL_TO_RESOLVE : bool = false;
pub const LEGACY_ALIASES_ARE_DECLARED_AT : str = "turbobaby/deeplink";

pub fn route_resolves(path_is_named: bool, catchall_present: bool) bool {
  return path_is_named or catchall_present;
}

; --- Tests -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

test the_instrument_is_declared_before_the_measurements {
  assert HOST_SUITE_COMPILES_THIS_HALF == false;
  assert a_claim_here_rests_on_a_test(HOST_SUITE_COMPILES_THIS_HALF) == false;
  assert CFG_TEST_MODULES_IN_UI == 5;
  assert UNIT_TESTS_NEVER_COMPILED == 32;
  assert SHIPPED_INSTRUMENT_IS_A_TEXT_SCAN == true;
  assert SCAN_NEEDLE_COUNT == 4;
  assert SCAN_SEES_A_DEFAULTED_ZERO == false;
}

test the_survey_cited_the_wasm_gate_one_line_above_the_attribute {
  assert WASM_GATE_SITE == "src/lib.rs:17";
  assert SURVEY_CITED_THE_GATE_AT == "src/lib.rs:16";
  assert WASM_GATE_SITE != SURVEY_CITED_THE_GATE_AT;
}

test every_reuse_edge_names_an_owner_and_not_a_line {
  assert REUSES_REQUEST_IDENTITY_ID == "turbobaby/request-identity";
  assert REUSES_CATALOG_API_ID == "turbobaby/catalog-api";
  assert REUSES_COMMERCE_ID == "turbobaby/commerce";
  assert REUSES_CLIENT_ERRORS_ID == "turbobaby/client-errors";
  assert REUSES_DEEPLINK_ID == "turbobaby/deeplink";
  assert REUSE_EDGE_COUNT == 5;
  assert REUSES_REQUEST_IDENTITY_ID != ID;
  assert REUSES_COMMERCE_ID != REUSES_CATALOG_API_ID;
  assert REUSES_DEEPLINK_ID != REUSES_CLIENT_ERRORS_ID;
}

test nothing_a_sibling_owns_is_copied_here {
  assert CAP_VALUE_IS_RESTATED_HERE == false;
  assert HEADER_LITERAL_IS_RESTATED_HERE == false;
  assert IDEMPOTENCY_ARMS_ARE_RESTATED_HERE == false;
  assert ROUTE_ALIASES_ARE_RESTATED_HERE == false;
  assert SIZE_CAP_IS_OWNED_BY == "turbobaby/request-identity";
  assert HEADER_NAME_IS_ALREADY_DECLARED_AT == "turbobaby/loyalty-ledger";
  assert LEGACY_ALIASES_ARE_DECLARED_AT == "turbobaby/deeplink";
}

test init_data_has_exactly_three_origins {
  assert init_data_origin(true, true, true) == ORIGIN_SIGNED;
  assert init_data_origin(true, true, false) == ORIGIN_SIGNED;
  assert init_data_origin(true, false, true) == ORIGIN_REBUILT;
  assert init_data_origin(true, false, false) == ORIGIN_NONE;
  assert init_data_origin(false, true, true) == ORIGIN_NONE;
  assert origin_is_known(ORIGIN_COUNT) == false;
}

test a_browser_tab_with_no_host_yields_an_empty_string_not_an_error {
  assert init_data_payload_is_empty(init_data_origin(false, false, false)) == true;
  assert init_data_payload_is_empty(ORIGIN_SIGNED) == false;
  assert init_data_payload_is_empty(ORIGIN_REBUILT) == false;
  assert ABSENT_HOST_YIELDS_AN_EMPTY_STRING == true;
  assert ABSENT_HOST_YIELDS_AN_ERROR == false;
}

test only_the_signed_string_is_a_proof {
  assert init_data_can_prove_identity(ORIGIN_SIGNED) == true;
  assert init_data_can_prove_identity(ORIGIN_REBUILT) == false;
  assert init_data_can_prove_identity(ORIGIN_NONE) == false;
  assert REBUILT_PAYLOAD_IS_SENT_ANYWAY == true;
  assert REBUILT_PAYLOAD_CAN_VERIFY == false;
}

test an_absent_bridge_does_not_stop_the_call {
  assert call_is_attempted(ORIGIN_NONE) == true;
  assert ABSENT_BRIDGE_BLOCKS_THE_CALL == false;
  assert refusal_comes_from_the_server(ORIGIN_NONE, true) == true;
  assert refusal_comes_from_the_server(ORIGIN_REBUILT, true) == true;
  assert refusal_comes_from_the_server(ORIGIN_SIGNED, true) == false;
  assert EMPTINESS_TEST_SITES == 2;
  assert HELPERS_THAT_SEND_AN_EMPTY_HEADER == 7;
}

test the_label_is_false_for_a_proof_and_for_an_absence_alike {
  assert reconstruction_label(ORIGIN_SIGNED) == false;
  assert reconstruction_label(ORIGIN_NONE) == false;
  assert reconstruction_label(ORIGIN_REBUILT) == true;
  assert LABEL_ALONE_SEPARATES_ABSENCE_FROM_PROOF == false;
}

test the_receiver_needs_the_label_and_the_emptiness_together {
  assert origin_recovered_by_receiver(false, true) == ORIGIN_NONE;
  assert origin_recovered_by_receiver(true, true) == ORIGIN_NONE;
  assert origin_recovered_by_receiver(false, false) == ORIGIN_SIGNED;
  assert origin_recovered_by_receiver(true, false) == ORIGIN_REBUILT;
}

test two_of_nine_sites_hand_the_cohort_a_false_input {
  assert AUTH_HEADER_SITES == 9;
  assert SITES_SENDING_THE_LABEL == 7;
  assert SITES_OMITTING_THE_LABEL == 2;
  assert UNLABELLED_SITES[0] == "src/ui/api/http.rs:368";
  assert UNLABELLED_SITES[1] == "src/ui/api/client.rs:63";
  assert cohort_input_is_faithful(ORIGIN_REBUILT, true) == true;
  assert cohort_input_is_faithful(ORIGIN_REBUILT, false) == false;
  assert cohort_input_is_faithful(ORIGIN_SIGNED, false) == true;
  assert cohort_input_is_faithful(ORIGIN_NONE, false) == true;
}

test an_oversize_payload_is_downgraded_and_not_refused {
  assert oversize_becomes_anonymous(true, false) == true;
  assert oversize_becomes_anonymous(true, true) == false;
  assert oversize_becomes_anonymous(false, false) == false;
  assert CLIENT_CAP_SITES == 1;
  assert CAP_APPLIES_TO_THE_FREE_HELPERS == false;
  assert OVERSIZE_IS_REFUSED_LOUDLY_ON_THE_CLIENT == false;
}

test exactly_one_call_retries_and_it_is_not_in_the_transport {
  assert RETRIED_CALL_COUNT == 1;
  assert RETRY_LIVES_IN_THE_TRANSPORT == false;
  assert MANUAL_RETRY_BUTTON_SCREENS == 3;
  assert MANUAL_RETRY_IS_AN_AUTOMATIC_RESEND == false;
  assert MANUAL_RETRY_BUTTON_SCREENS > RETRIED_CALL_COUNT;
  assert ATTEMPT_MAX == 4;
  assert BACKOFF_STEP_COUNT == 3;
  assert BACKOFF_MS[0] == 1000;
  assert BACKOFF_MS[1] == 2000;
  assert BACKOFF_MS[2] == 4000;
  assert ATTEMPTS_CLAIMED_BY_THE_DOC_COMMENT == 3;
  assert ATTEMPTS_CLAIMED_BY_THE_DOC_COMMENT != ATTEMPT_MAX;
  assert DOC_COMMENT_AGREES_WITH_THE_LOOP == false;
  assert ATTEMPTS_CLAIMED_BY_THE_DOC_COMMENT + 1 == ATTEMPT_MAX;
}

test only_a_network_error_or_a_server_status_is_retried {
  assert attempt_is_retried(CLASS_NETWORK) == true;
  assert attempt_is_retried(CLASS_SERVER) == true;
  assert attempt_is_retried(CLASS_SUCCESS) == false;
  assert attempt_is_retried(CLASS_CONFLICT) == false;
  assert attempt_is_retried(CLASS_OTHER_STATUS) == false;
  assert response_class_is_known(CLASS_SERVER) == true;
  assert response_class_is_known(RESPONSE_CLASS_COUNT) == false;
}

test a_terminal_class_spends_one_attempt_and_a_retried_class_spends_four {
  assert attempts_used(CLASS_SUCCESS) == 1;
  assert attempts_used(CLASS_CONFLICT) == 1;
  assert attempts_used(CLASS_OTHER_STATUS) == 1;
  assert attempts_used(CLASS_NETWORK) == 4;
  assert attempts_used(CLASS_SERVER) == 4;
}

test the_first_attempt_does_not_wait {
  assert backoff_before(0) == 0;
  assert backoff_before(1) == 1000;
  assert backoff_before(2) == 2000;
  assert backoff_before(3) == 4000;
  assert FIRST_ATTEMPT_WAITS == false;
}

test the_retry_cannot_duplicate_a_write_because_the_screen_holds_the_key {
  assert retry_can_duplicate_a_write(true, true) == false;
  assert retry_can_duplicate_a_write(true, false) == true;
  assert retry_can_duplicate_a_write(false, true) == true;
  assert retry_can_duplicate_a_write(false, false) == true;
  assert KEY_IS_MINTED_BY_THE_TRANSPORT == false;
  assert KEY_WRITE_SITES == 1;
}

test one_write_site_is_also_why_an_edited_cart_reuses_the_key {
  assert KEY_ROTATES_WHEN_THE_PAYLOAD_CHANGES == false;
  assert resubmission_reuses_a_key_with_a_new_payload(true, true, true) == true;
  assert resubmission_reuses_a_key_with_a_new_payload(true, false, true) == false;
  assert resubmission_reuses_a_key_with_a_new_payload(true, true, false) == false;
  assert IDEMPOTENCY_VERDICT_INPUT == "commerce_idempotency_decision, supplied by the commerce contract";
}

test the_client_cannot_tell_a_replay_from_a_new_order {
  assert SERVER_REPLAY_STATUS == 200;
  assert SERVER_REPLAY_FLAG_NAME == "idempotent_replay";
  assert CLIENT_READS_THE_REPLAY_FLAG == false;
  assert client_distinguishes_replay_from_create(CLIENT_READS_THE_REPLAY_FLAG) == false;
  assert client_distinguishes_replay_from_create(true) == true;
}

test the_conflict_arm_guards_a_status_the_endpoint_never_sends {
  assert ORDER_CREATE_EVER_RETURNS_409 == false;
  assert conflict_branch_can_fire(ORDER_CREATE_EVER_RETURNS_409) == false;
  assert conflict_branch_can_fire(true) == true;
  assert CONFLICT_RECOVERY_IS_POSITIONAL == true;
  assert CONFLICT_RECOVERY_MATCHES_THE_KEY == false;
  assert recovered_order_is_provably_ours(CONFLICT_RECOVERY_MATCHES_THE_KEY) == false;
}

test no_deadline_is_declared_because_none_is_implemented {
  assert REQUEST_DEADLINE_IS_SHIPPED == false;
  assert ABORT_OCCURRENCES_IN_UI == 0;
  assert request_can_hang_until_the_browser_gives_up(false) == true;
  assert request_can_hang_until_the_browser_gives_up(true) == false;
}

test the_mirror_counts_add_up {
  assert DTO_FIELD_COUNT == 172;
  assert DTO_FIELDS_WITH_A_DEFAULT == 44;
  assert DEFAULTS_ON_AN_OPTION == 27;
  assert DEFAULTS_ON_A_BARE_NUMBER == 7;
  assert DEFAULTS_ON_A_BOOL_STRING_OR_VEC == 10;
  assert DEFAULTS_ON_AN_OPTION + DEFAULTS_ON_A_BARE_NUMBER + DEFAULTS_ON_A_BOOL_STRING_OR_VEC == DTO_FIELDS_WITH_A_DEFAULT;
  assert FIELDS_THAT_BREAK_LOUDLY == 128;
  assert DTO_STRUCT_COUNT == 24;
  assert DTO_ENUM_COUNT == 3;
}

test a_dropped_field_is_loud_only_when_it_has_no_default {
  assert dropped_field_breaks_the_client(false) == true;
  assert dropped_field_breaks_the_client(true) == false;
  assert dropped_field_renders_an_invented_value(true, true) == true;
  assert dropped_field_renders_an_invented_value(true, false) == false;
  assert dropped_field_renders_an_invented_value(false, true) == false;
  assert mirror_is_faithful(false, true) == true;
  assert mirror_is_faithful(true, true) == false;
  assert MIRROR_RULE_HOLDS_ON_EVERY_FIELD == false;
}

test the_seven_numeric_default_sites_are_named {
  assert NUMERIC_DEFAULT_SITES[0] == "src/ui/api/types.rs:28";
  assert NUMERIC_DEFAULT_SITES[3] == "src/ui/api/types.rs:421";
  assert NUMERIC_DEFAULT_SITES[4] == "src/ui/api/types.rs:423";
  assert NUMERIC_DEFAULT_SITES[5] == "src/ui/api/types.rs:435";
  assert NUMERIC_DEFAULT_SITES[6] == "src/ui/api/types.rs:446";
}

test the_cart_drops_two_unreadable_things_and_keeps_the_third {
  assert cart_line_survives(true, true) == true;
  assert cart_line_survives(false, true) == false;
  assert cart_line_survives(true, false) == false;
  assert LINE_DROPPED_ON_UNKNOWN_KIND == true;
  assert LINE_DROPPED_ON_ZERO_QUANTITY == true;
  assert LINE_DROPPED_ON_AN_ABSENT_PRICE == false;
}

test an_absent_price_is_the_one_absence_nothing_shows {
  assert price_absence_is_visible(false, true) == true;
  assert price_absence_is_visible(true, false) == true;
  assert price_absence_is_visible(true, true) == false;
  assert ABSENT_PRICE_SURVIVES_AS_A_FREE_LINE == true;
  assert NON_FINITE_PRICE_SURVIVES_AS_A_FREE_LINE == true;
}

test the_route_table_always_resolves {
  assert ROUTE_ARM_COUNT == 26;
  assert NAMED_ROUTE_COUNT == 25;
  assert CATCHALL_ROUTE_COUNT == 1;
  assert NAMED_ROUTE_COUNT + CATCHALL_ROUTE_COUNT == ROUTE_ARM_COUNT;
  assert route_resolves(true, true) == true;
  assert route_resolves(false, true) == true;
  assert route_resolves(false, false) == false;
  assert ROUTE_TABLE_CAN_FAIL_TO_RESOLVE == false;
}

; --- Invariants ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------

invariant no_claim_in_this_file_rests_on_a_compiled_test
  assert a_claim_here_rests_on_a_test(HOST_SUITE_COMPILES_THIS_HALF) == false and UNIT_TESTS_NEVER_COMPILED == 32

invariant a_rebuilt_payload_is_never_a_proof
  assert init_data_can_prove_identity(ORIGIN_REBUILT) == false and REBUILT_PAYLOAD_CAN_VERIFY == false

invariant an_absent_host_is_never_a_proof
  assert init_data_can_prove_identity(init_data_origin(false, true, true)) == false

invariant the_label_alone_cannot_separate_an_absence_from_a_proof
  assert reconstruction_label(ORIGIN_SIGNED) == reconstruction_label(ORIGIN_NONE) and LABEL_ALONE_SEPARATES_ABSENCE_FROM_PROOF == false

invariant an_unlabelled_rebuild_misinforms_the_cohort
  assert cohort_input_is_faithful(ORIGIN_REBUILT, false) == false and SITES_OMITTING_THE_LABEL == 2

invariant a_successful_response_is_never_retried
  assert attempt_is_retried(CLASS_SUCCESS) == false and attempts_used(CLASS_SUCCESS) == 1

invariant a_conflict_is_never_retried
  assert attempt_is_retried(CLASS_CONFLICT) == false

invariant the_attempt_ceiling_is_the_loop_and_not_the_comment
  assert attempts_used(CLASS_SERVER) == ATTEMPT_MAX and ATTEMPTS_CLAIMED_BY_THE_DOC_COMMENT + 1 == ATTEMPT_MAX and DOC_COMMENT_AGREES_WITH_THE_LOOP == false

invariant no_attempt_beyond_the_first_is_immediate
  assert backoff_before(0) == 0 and backoff_before(1) == 1000 and backoff_before(2) == 2000 and backoff_before(3) == 4000

invariant a_retry_with_a_stable_attached_key_cannot_write_twice
  assert retry_can_duplicate_a_write(KEY_IS_ATTACHED_ON_THE_RETRIED_CALL, true) == false

invariant a_missing_key_makes_every_retry_a_possible_duplicate
  assert retry_can_duplicate_a_write(false, true) == true

invariant the_conflict_arm_is_unreachable_from_the_endpoint_it_guards
  assert conflict_branch_can_fire(ORDER_CREATE_EVER_RETURNS_409) == false

invariant a_recovered_order_that_does_not_match_the_key_is_not_provably_ours
  assert recovered_order_is_provably_ours(CONFLICT_RECOVERY_MATCHES_THE_KEY) == false

invariant no_deadline_is_invented_where_none_is_shipped
  assert REQUEST_DEADLINE_IS_SHIPPED == false and ABORT_OCCURRENCES_IN_UI == 0

invariant a_defaulted_number_is_the_only_silent_drop
  assert dropped_field_renders_an_invented_value(true, true) == true and dropped_field_renders_an_invented_value(false, true) == false and dropped_field_breaks_the_client(false) == true

invariant the_default_partition_is_complete
  assert DEFAULTS_ON_AN_OPTION + DEFAULTS_ON_A_BARE_NUMBER + DEFAULTS_ON_A_BOOL_STRING_OR_VEC == DTO_FIELDS_WITH_A_DEFAULT

invariant a_surviving_line_with_a_defaulted_price_hides_the_absence
  assert price_absence_is_visible(true, true) == false and ABSENT_PRICE_SURVIVES_AS_A_FREE_LINE == true

invariant a_dropped_line_is_a_visible_absence
  assert price_absence_is_visible(false, true) == true

invariant the_catchall_is_what_makes_the_route_table_total
  assert route_resolves(false, true) == true and route_resolves(false, false) == false

invariant every_edge_names_an_owner_that_is_not_this_file
  assert REUSES_REQUEST_IDENTITY_ID != ID and REUSES_CATALOG_API_ID != ID and REUSES_COMMERCE_ID != ID and REUSES_CLIENT_ERRORS_ID != ID and REUSES_DEEPLINK_ID != ID
